@startuml
title State and Singleton implementation
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName DejaVu Sans
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam ArrowColor #334155
skinparam classBorderColor #334155
skinparam classBackgroundColor #EFF6FF
skinparam linetype ortho
hide empty members

class EmbeddedSystemX <<Context>> {
    -state_ : State*
    -mode_ : State*
    -name_ : string
    -versionNo_ : int
    -errorNo_ : int
    +Start()
    +chMode1()
    +chMode2()
    +displayState()
    -dispatch(handler, event)
    -transitionTo(next)
    -setMode(mode)
}

abstract class State {
    +{abstract} name() : string_view
    +onEntry(context)
    +Start(context)
    +Restart(context)
    +chMode1(context)
    +chMode2(context)
    +eventX(context)
}

class PowerOnSelfTest <<Singleton>> {
    +{static} instance()
    +SelftestOk(context)
    +SelfTestFailed(context, errorNo)
}
class Initializing <<Singleton>> {
    +{static} instance()
    +Initialized(context)
}
class Failure <<Singleton>> {
    +{static} instance()
    +Restart(context)
    +Exit(context)
}
class Operational <<Singleton>> {
    +{static} instance()
    +onEntry(context)
    +Restart(context)
}
class Ready <<Singleton>> {
    +{static} instance()
    +Start(context)
    +Configure(context)
}
class Configuration <<Singleton>> {
    +{static} instance()
    +ConfigX(context)
    +ConfigurationEnded(context)
}
class RealTimeLoop <<Singleton>> {
    +{static} instance()
    +Stop(context)
    +chMode1(context)
    +chMode2(context)
    +eventX(context)
}
class Mode1 <<Singleton>> {
    +{static} instance()
    +chMode2(context)
    +eventX(context)
}
class Mode2 <<Singleton>> {
    +{static} instance()
    +chMode1(context)
    +eventX(context)
}

EmbeddedSystemX --> State : state_ / mode_
State <|-- PowerOnSelfTest
State <|-- Initializing
State <|-- Failure
State <|-- Operational
State <|-- Mode1
State <|-- Mode2
Operational <|-- Ready
Operational <|-- Configuration
Operational <|-- RealTimeLoop

note top of State
  Selected operations are shown.
  All event handlers have an ignored-event default.
  Concrete states override their accepted events.
end note
note bottom of Operational
  Ready, Configuration and RealTimeLoop inherit Restart.
  Entering Operational immediately enters Ready.
end note
note bottom of Mode2
  Each context stores its own active mode and error data.
  Concrete singleton states have static lifetime.
end note
@enduml
